            <ArticleTitle>The changing face of peptic ulcer in the elderly.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1159-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The elderly patient presents a challenge to the physician both in recognition of peptic ulcer disease and in long term management. Only with close observation and an awareness of the higher complication rate can a successful therapeutic approach be developed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
